      "title": "Faculty | Hendrix College",
      "description": "Faculty | Hendrix College Faculty | Hendrix College Skip to content Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents Alumni News Events Give Admission & Aid Back to Main Menu Admission & Aid Admission & Aid Overview Admissions Requirements Transfer Students International Applicants Affording Hendrix Financial Aid Visit The road to your future goes through Hendrix. Request Info Academics Back to Main Menu Academics Academics Overview Departments and Majors Advising Co-ops For All Student Research Via Hendrix Our Faculty Study Abroad Bailey Library Hendrix-Murphy Foundation From the first year through graduation, Integrated Advising is a vital part of our mission. Discover Integrated Advising Life at Hendrix Back to Main Menu Life at Hendrix Life at Hendrix Overview Campus Traditions Orientation New Students Living on Campus Dining Services Student Activities Health & Well-being The Arts From legendary campus events to everyday celebrations, see how we build a community where everyone belongs. Explore Hendrix Traditions Athletics After Hendrix Back to Main Menu After Hendrix After Hendrix Overview Career Success Outcomes Alumni No matter your major, step out of the classroom and get the real-world career experience you need to stand out. Co-op Experiences About Back to Main Menu About About Overview President Leadership Accreditation Around Campus About Conway Enjoy the perfect balance of small-town charm, outdoor adventure, and capital-city culture right outside your front door. Get to Know Conway Search Hendrix College Top Searches VIA Hendrix Campus Map Directory Academic Calendar Affording Hendrix Housing Home Academics The Faculty The Faculty Related Topics Related Topics Centers and Programs Degree Requirements Departments and Majors Go Further Via Hendrix Study Abroad The Faculty Via Hendrix Mentors, Scholars, and Champions for Your Success Your professors at Hendrix College are more than lecturers. They are people you can turn to for guidance throughout your time here. Whether you need help understanding course material, exploring career paths, or finding a sounding board for your innovative ideas, they are here for you from the moment you step foot on campus. Our professors are academic experts and also are deeply invested in your success. They teach at Hendrix because they consider your growth a core part of their work, not an added responsibility. Request Information Why the Hendrix Faculty Stand Out Skilled faculty. Mentors who help you set and achieve your goals. At Hendrix, they are one and the same. 93% Faculty Members With the Highest Degree in Their Field Almost all of our faculty have a Ph.D. or the terminal degree in their field. So you will learn directly from scholars advancing their fields. 13:1 Student-Faculty Ratio Small class sizes help you make real connections with faculty, allowing you to exchange ideas and ask questions. 100% Of Academic Advisors Are Full-Time Faculty Because your advisor understands the curriculum and your goals, they can help you create a personalized academic experience. Integrated Advising #59 Best Undergraduate Teaching Among National Liberal Arts Colleges Our faculty are dedicated to the craft of teaching — and other college administrators surveyed by U.S. News & World Report agree. 1 of 1 Integrated Advising: Navigating Via Hendrix You are going to do great things. Your personal advising team, which includes a faculty member as your academic advisor, will help you chart a path to get there. That collaboration is a core element of Via Hendrix, our career-readiness curriculum. Explore Via Hendrix Meet the Hendrix Faculty While teaching comes first, our faculty are also experts in everything from robotics to racial injustice and poetry to psychophysiology. Learn more about them here: All Hendrix Faculty Guiding Your Way Via Hendrix At Hendrix, who teaches you is just as important as what you learn. Request Information Visit Apply Hendrix College 1600 Washington Avenue Conway, Arkansas 72032 501-329-6811 Contact Us Quick Links Maps & Directions Directory Calendars Jobs Spirit Store Campus Web Web Mail Celebrating 150 Years Founded in 1876, Hendrix College is a Conway-based liberal arts school. Support Hendrix College Back to Top Copyright © 2026 Hendrix College Privacy Title IX Campus Safety Nondiscrimination Your Way Forward Via Hendrix Request Info Visit Apply"
    },
    "https://via.hendrix.edu/after-hendrix/career-success": {
      "title": "Career Success",
      "description": "Career Success | Hendrix College Career Success | Hendrix College Skip to content Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents Alumni News Events Give Admission & Aid Back to Main Menu Admission & Aid Admission & Aid Overview Admissions Requirements Transfer Students International Applicants Affording Hendrix Financial Aid Visit The road to your future goes through Hendrix. Request Info Academics Back to Main Menu Academics Academics Overview Departments and Majors Advising Co-ops For All Student Research Via Hendrix Our Faculty Study Abroad Bailey Library Hendrix-Murphy Foundation From the first year through graduation, Integrated Advising is a vital part of our mission. Discover Integrated Advising Life at Hendrix Back to Main Menu Life at Hendrix Life at Hendrix Overview Campus Traditions Orientation New Students Living on Campus Dining Services Student Activities Health & Well-being The Arts From legendary campus events to everyday celebrations, see how we build a community where everyone belongs. Explore Hendrix Traditions Athletics After Hendrix Back to Main Menu After Hendrix After Hendrix Overview Career Success Outcomes Alumni No matter your major, step out of the classroom and get the real-world career experience you need to stand out. Co-op Experiences About Back to Main Menu About About Overview President Leadership Accreditation Around Campus About Conway Enjoy the perfect balance of small-town charm, outdoor adventure, and capital-city culture right outside your front door. Get to Know Conway Search Hendrix College Top Searches VIA Hendrix Campus Map Directory Academic Calendar Affording Hendrix Housing Home After Hendrix Career Success Career Success Related Topics Related Topics Alumni Career Connections Recruiters On This Page On This Page Via Hendrix Your Next Four Years First Year Sophomore Year Junior Year Senior Year Career Competencies Employers At Hendrix, you’re not just picking a major, you’re building a toolkit for the future. We give you the tools to explore everything from liberal arts to the sciences, all while helping you along the way. Meet With Career Success Staff Work Study Jobs through HireHendrix Internships Info for Recruiters Alumni Career Connections Via Hendrix Via Hendrix is a comprehensive initiative to incorporate career preparation throughout its undergraduate liberal arts curriculum, introducing a semester-long professional experience for all students. All students will complete a cooperative education, or co-op, which involves professional work or research placements as part of their degree program. Students will gain hands-on experience in their prospective fields which will increase their job extensions post grad. While many schools offer internships, those are typically optional, shorter, and less intensive. The Via Hendrix co-op strategy features a 12- to 14-week immersion. Students prepare their first year; each will receive an integrated advising team to provide academic and professional support through graduation. Co-op companies include health care providers, professional sports teams, law firms, nonprofit organizations, government entities, and more. “Co-op is an extension of the liberal arts classroom, building our learning experiences out into the professional world,” said Hendrix President Karen Petersen. “Via Hendrix will create a real-time, continuous feedback loop with employers of all types, giving us powerful insight to adjust over time and to foster a talent pipeline for partner organizations that host our students.” In their fourth and final year, students will reflect on the totality of their experience as they work with their integrated advising teams to apply for jobs or graduate school. Get to Know Via Hendrix Your Next Four Years One size does NOT fit all! Your journey at Hendrix may not look like the plan below, and that’s OK. These are some suggested activities to help you hit the ground running and finish strong as you grow in your time at Hendrix. No matter what you plan to do after graduation, Career Services can help! First Year Check Daily / Weekly Check Daily / Weekly Check your Hendrix email EVERY day. Use your HDX Today app to read Hendrix Today AT LEAST 2-3 times/week. Follow Hendrix Career Services on Instagram @hendrixcareer . Explore multiple majors or search for information about your chosen field with the “What Can I Do With This Major” button below. What Can I Do With This Major? Job and Career Search Time to Meet Time to Meet Meet with your professors outside of class. Meet with Career Success to explore majors and career options. Schedule a meeting to get to know your advisor. Meet with your integrated advising team which includes Career Success. Meet with Career Success Branch Out Branch Out Join a campus organization or start volunteering with a local non profit. Participate in an internship this summer (after your first year) Volunteer with Local Non-Profits More Volunteer Opportunities Follow Us Sophomore Year Year two brings further exploration into your major! You’ll expand your horizons by making connections, generating quality research, and harnessing resources available to you. Questions will arise and we are here to help. Time to Meet Time to Meet Meet with Career Success to explore your chosen major and how it relates to careers. Meet with Career Success in your spring semester to find an internship and begin looking into your prospective co-op. EVST and HESC students who started at Hendrix before the 2026-27 academic year: You will need to complete an internship before graduation. Meet with Career Success Check it Out Check it Out Check out the Career Explorer and Career Finder found in HireHendrix ; you can take a quiz and get career suggestions then do a deep dive into specific industries and careers. Build alumni connections through HCAN and FACT Fridays. Visit the Study Abroad Office and/or the Study Abroad Fair. Explore undergraduate research opportunities if considering medical school or graduate school. Connect with Alumni Study Abroad Office HireHendrix Junior Year This year is all about being proactive and defining your path. Your steps will bring you to leadership opportunities, professional associations, and/or further education. Take your previous preparation and watch it blossom this year. Participate Participate Complete your co-op by the spring of this year. Become a leader in one or more campus organizations. Join a professional association if graduate or professional school is in your future. Extending Your Learning Extending Your Learning If planning to attend graduate school, explore graduate programs and meet with your advisor to develop a concrete plan. If a pre-med, do medical school interview preparation and work on personal statements with Pre-Med Advising Committee and your advisor. Senior Year Welcome to the finish line! Your hard work is about to pay off. As you prepare for graduation, you’ll prepare any application materials, polish your resume, and start looking at potential job openings. Final Preparations Final Preparations Update your resume. (Do you need a CV?) Practice writing a cover letter. Schedule a mock interview with Career Success. Participate in a final internship or research opportunity. Begin job search, prepare your application materials, and let us know if you need assistance! Internships Resume Writing Resources We’re Always Here to Help We’re Always Here to Help Have Career Success review your application materials before you submit them. After you graduate, Hendrix Career Success is STILL here for you! See our Alumni page. Meet with Career Success Alumni Career Connections Career Competencies Hendrix College cultivates graduates who are ready to engage with the world beyond our campus. Embracing eight Career Competencies, our entire community works together to inspire graduates to live lives of accomplishment, integrity, service, and joy. Cultivate Eight Career Competencies With the guidance of the college community and the curriculum requirements, our students benefit from the breadth and depth of a liberal arts and sciences education combined with career readiness components. Career Competencies Catalog & Careers Career Planning Explore our Academic Catalog and the real-world application of each major as well as examples of internships, graduate schools, and employment outcomes of students and recent grads. Academic Catalog Career Readiness Employers Looking to partner with Hendrix and provide co-ops for our students? Explore how we can help connect our students with your company. Via Hendrix integrates a comprehensive initiative to incorporate career preparation throughout its undergraduate liberal arts curriculum, introducing a semester-long work experience for all students. All students will complete a immersive education experience, or co-op, which involves professional or research placements as part of their degree program. Partner with Hendrix Recruiter Tabling Form Visit Us Whether you are a local to Central Arkansas or a reach across the map, we are here to help plan your Hendrix College visit today! After viewing our campus video, download the campus map to navigate our campus, then meet with us so we can provide resources to help pave the path to your future career. Meet with Us Campus Map Office of Career Success Staff Julie Agee Gillaspy Executive Director of Career Success Email: Gillaspy@hendrix.edu Office Phone: (501) 450-1236 Office Location: Career Success, SLTC 245 Leigh Lassiter-Counts Director of Career Success Email: lassiter-counts@hendrix.edu Office Phone: (501) 450-1439 Office Location: Career Success, SLTC 242 Tricia Burris Assistant Director of Career Success Email: burris@hendrix.edu Office Phone: (501) 450-1373 Office Location: Career Services, SLTC 241 Gabriel Foreman Career Counselor Email: ForemanG@hendrix.edu Office Phone: (501) 329-6811 Office Location: Career Success, SLTC 225 1 of 2 Contact the Office of Career Success Reach out to Career Success by email, phone, or in-person. Career Success staff are located in the Hendrix Student Life and Technology Center on the second floor in 241, 242, and 245. Phone 501-450-1440 Email career@hendrix.edu Mailing Address Office of Career Success 1600 Washington Avenue Conway, AR 72032-3080 Follow Us on Instagram Hendrix College 1600 Washington Avenue Conway, Arkansas 72032 501-329-6811 Contact Us Quick Links Maps & Directions Directory Calendars Jobs Spirit Store Campus Web Web Mail Celebrating 150 Years Founded in 1876, Hendrix College is a Conway-based liberal arts school. Support Hendrix College Back to Top Copyright © 2026 Hendrix College Privacy Title IX Campus Safety Nondiscrimination Your Way Forward Via Hendrix Request Info Visit Apply"
    }
